{title: A Room Prepared for Me}
{subtitle: John 14:2}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Bb/D] | [Cm] |
| [Ab] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Do not let your hearts be [Bb/D]troubled
You be[Cm]lieve in God, [Ab]believe in me
[Eb]In my Father's house are [Bb/D]many rooms
[Cm]If it [Cm7/Bb]were not so, would [Ab]I have told [Bb]you
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
There's a [Eb]room pre[Bb]pared for [Cm]me
[Cm7/Bb]In my [Ab]Father's house up yon[Bb]der
I will [Eb]go and he [Bb/D]will come a[Cm]gain
[Cm7/Bb]And [Ab]take me home [Bb]to be with [Eb]him [Bb/D]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]I go to prepare a place [Bb/D]for you
[Cm]And if I go, I'll [Ab]come again
And [Eb]take you to myself, [Bb/D]that where I am
[Ab]There you may be also, my [Bb]friend
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
There's a [Eb]room pre[Bb]pared for [Cm]me
[Cm7/Bb]In my [Ab]Father's house up yon[Bb]der
I will [Eb]go and he [Bb/D]will come a[Cm]gain
[Cm7/Bb]And [Ab]take me home [Bb]to be with [Eb]him [Bb/D][Eb]
{end_of_chorus}
